// THE E1 UNIT (design p4261-e1-b): its bench records, phases, incidents and its own fault
// hypotheses.

// PIN 7 IS HELD AT 0 V; Q301, HELD ON, IS THE LEADING CANDIDATE. Read on its own lead at 48 V, pin 7 is
// far below its threshold (controller_enable_standing), so the input stage is held off by its enable. Unpowered, the
// lead's path to ground is one-way, and its node reaches bare pads on the back; no in-circuit
// resistance names a part on it, and arithmetic over two such readings is a lead for a direct reading,
// never a component's value (product.electrical.measured_netlist).
data p4261_enable_network_hypothesis: InvestigationHypothesis = InvestigationHypothesis {
  claim: "U1_P5's UVLO/EN (pin 7) reads 0 V with the source at 48 V, read with the probe on its own lead: below its 2.41 V minimum, so the tested configuration has not shown a permissive enable input and the input stage is held off by its enable. The leading candidate for what holds it is Q301, held on with nothing to release it: at 54 V, Q301's lead b node reads about 4.9 V and the far end of the resistor feeding it 54 V, the input itself; Q300's lead b -- the input that would pull Q301's lead b down -- reads 0 V; and P6, on Q301's lone lead, reads 0 V. Under the candidate BSS138 pinout (K38) that is Q300 off, Q301 on and P6 at the return; P6 is pin 7's by the operator's ruling and the third wire's signature, not by a reading, and Q300's lead b, followed by eye toward U51, is where an enable would arrive. Other causes stay live: P6 not being pin 7's node after all, another pull-down, no pull-up to raise pin 7 once Q301 releases it, another protection or logic condition, or damage from the probe incident",
  sources: [
    "energized at 48 V with nothing wired to the chip, the probe held on the leads: pin 8 about 1.8 V -- what its back-side pad read at 48 V, so the count from the pin 1 marker holds -- and pin 7 0 V (controller_enable_standing). A probe touching nothing also reads 0 V; pin 8 was read the same way just before. One source setting, so whether pin 7 moves with the input is unread (enable_projection)",
    "Q21_P5 and Q22_P5 read blocking at 48 V (input_switch_standing), and U1_P5's OVLO reads below its 2.39 V minimum at 48 V on its own lead (controller_overvoltage_standing), as the pad reported on pin 8 (no baseline recorded) did at 48 V and 36 V: overvoltage lockout is not what holds it off. TI SNVS950C's design example, section 9.2.1.2.6 option B (R3 = 95.3 kohm, R4 = 3.74 kohm), predicts the OVLO readings -- a reference circuit, not this board's parts",
    "unpowered, pin 7's own lead to J20's black lead: over range on the 200 ohm range both ways; about 535 ohm with the red probe on J20's lead; over range on the 2k range and about 11 kohm on the 20k range with the red probe on pin 7. The path is one-way; which way it conducts waits on this meter's resistance-mode polarity, which is unverified. The first wire read the same pattern to the ground pad, consistent with its having been on pin 7 then -- still no join of it, and its later readings stay disputed (e1_pin7_attachment)",
    "a close photograph of U1_P5's left-hand row, no wire on it, shows no solder bridge between leads 1 and 10; and a bridge to pin 8 or to ground would have read low from pin 7's lead",
    "unpowered, the ringed point RP1 right of U1_P5 read about 1.3 kohm from pin 7's own lead, the lowest the operator found near the lead on the front; no point near pin 7 on the front reads at the baseline to it",
    "a third wire, W4, taped at the left-hand row, reads pin 7's signature (about 11 kohm to ground with the red probe on it) and 16 kohm to pin 8's pad; three bare pads on the back beside Q5_P5 and D5_P5 (P5, P6, P7 of the labelled photograph) read 0 ohm from it, with no baseline recorded, and it still read about 12 kohm to ground afterwards. No reading joins W4 to the lead (the tape covers it), so P5 to P7 are pin 7's only by the wire's signature and by the operator's ruling of 2026-10-19 ('yes i am hyper confident that p6 == pin 7'), which settles the question in the record without being a reading. The cluster's pads carry no parts on the E1, and the same cluster is bare on the K1 (photograph, bench-session upload c21ab386): its empty places are the design's, not a part missing from the E1",
    "unpowered, the cluster's other pads read to J20's black lead, J20's red lead and VDD's point (the top end of pin 21's beige part): P10 is reported as ground (no baseline recorded); P1 to P4, P8 and P9 read above the baseline to all three. No pad of the cluster joins pin 7's pads to the return, the input or VDD directly, so its empty places are not a missing direct pull-up or pull-down to those; P9 beside the grounded P10 reads to none and did not read 0 from the third wire. Within about a centimetre on both faces, the third wire's node reaches only the three bare pads",
    "unpowered, the lone lead of Q301's three-lead package on the back reads 0.00 ohm to P6: the first fitted part found at P6, which no reading yet joins to pin 7's lead (it is pin 7's only by the third wire's signature and the operator's ruling). Q301's 'K38' marking is a candidate for Diodes Incorporated's BSS138, whose pinout puts the drain on the lone lead -- the open-drain device TI describes for holding UVLO/EN low -- a lead, not Q301's established role. Q300 and Q301 both carry the marking 'K38' (operator, photograph bench-session upload 42ffb97b); the code matches Diodes Incorporated's marking table, but no maker is read from the parts themselves, so neither's type nor pinout is established (e1_k38_candidate)",
    "unpowered, Q301's lead a reads 0 ohm and Q300's lead a 0.00 ohm to J20's return, and Q301's lead b 0.00 ohm to Q300's lone lead. No session recorded a shorted-probe baseline or the range, so these zeros, the third wire's to P5 to P7 and Q301's lone lead's to P6 are reported zeros, not joins (product.electrical.bench_session), and the netlist keeps each pair's points apart. Read as joins, Q300's lone lead drives Q301's lead b, and Q301's lone lead is on P6. Under the candidate BSS138 pinout with the silkscreen triangle on pin 1 -- lead b the gate, lead a the source, the lone lead the drain -- that is two N-channel low-side stages, Q300 able to pull Q301's gate to the return and Q301 able to pull P6 to it. The K38 identification is a candidate, so this shape is a lead, not the circuit's established role",
    "unpowered, the resistor beside Q301 has its nearer end reported equal to Q301's lead b ('==' and later '0.00ohm', no baseline recorded); its far end's trace, followed by eye, runs on the front toward D5's tab beside J20 and up past the bare U2_P5 and U3_P5 footprints toward U1_TSE beside J1, reading 0 ohm as far as about U2_P5 and about 2 kohm beyond (hedged, points named by place). The operator reads the layout as two input sides, J1's backplane and J20; with J20 energized at 54 V the far end reads 54 V",
    "energized, the via on Q301's lead b node (by the visible trace and a reported 0.0 ohm, not a baselined reading) reads about 3.8 V with the source at 38 V and about 4.9 V at 54 V, against J20's black lead: it rises with the input, not in proportion. If lead b is Q301's gate, as the candidate BSS138 pinout has it, a few volts there -- above that part's 1.5 V maximum gate threshold (DS30144) -- would switch Q301 on and hold P6 at the return, consistent with pin 7's 0 V if P6 is pin 7's node; and the voltage comes from the input itself, so with J20 energized the stage is held off unless Q300 pulls that node down",
    "energized at 54 V (2026-10-20), against J20's black lead: Q300's lead b 0 V, P6 0 V, and the far end of the resistor beside Q301 54 V -- the input. With the via's 4.9 V at 54 V, Q301's lead b sits near a tenth of the input, fed from it through that resistor, and Q300's lead b at 0 V says nothing drives Q300 on. These are readings at P6 and at the parts' pads, not at pin 7, which read 0 V at 48 V on its own lead",
    "unpowered (2026-10-20): across the resistor beside Q301, 26 kohm -- in circuit a resistor reads at or below its value, so it is at least about 26 kohm and '180' as 18 ohm is excluded; enlarged, its marking reads '18D', 150 kohm by the EIA-96 code, unresolved until the third character is confirmed (e1_q301_resistor). Q300's lead b reads 8 kohm to J20's black lead and 24 kohm to VDD's point; the via reads 0.0 to Q301's lead b. The zeros re-read (ZB2 to ZB6) name no dial position, and the shorted probes read '.005' and '.03 or something at 2k', so none of them joins",
    "Q300's lead b's trace, followed by eye on the back (bench-session upload 54ded557, drawn by hand), runs the length of the board to beside U51, a two-row package next to U49; no reading joins the trace's end to Q300's lead b. Both read 'LV165A / 2BKG4 / AEC0' (2026-10-20), TI's marking for the SN74LV165A parallel-load shift register: a part that reads eight inputs and shifts them out serially, with two serial outputs. Unpowered on the 20k range (2026-10-20), Q300's lead b reads 2.5 to 6 kohm to each of U51's pins 1 to 8, pin 8 (GND under SCLS402R) the same 2.5 kohm as J20's black lead, and the pin 8 pair moves with the range (about 600 ohm on 2k, 20 kohm on 200k; the first report of '20 ohm' was that 200k reading): a path holding a junction, not a join, so no U51 pin is read as the gate node's (q300_gate_path_reading). On the front, beside U92, the operator reports a point near U55 (sixteen terminals, marked 'ZVK' over '22J': a candidate SN74AVC4T774 level translator, extdeps.electronic_component.ti_sn74avc4t774, whose top edge under that pinout is DIR2, DIR1, VCCA, VCCB and no data port). Further along the front, a run of points each about 500 ohm from Q300's lead b on the 2k range: the pad beside Y50's upper corner, both ends of a small resistor beside U43, the capacitor at U43's right, and the lower pad of the part above U500, whose trace runs to U500's upper-right contact, itself 500 ohm; U500's other read contacts are 800 ohm (its ground, '0.00' to J20's black lead, no baseline) to 1.5 kohm, and the via beside the chain 800 ohm. Read each way, the pad reads 500 ohm to the return with red on it and 300 ohm swapped, and 500 then 1000 ohm to Q300's lead b, so these are paths holding junctions, not a resistor chain (pair_polarity_standing). So the gate's path to the return reads 800 ohm there, the 500 ohm points are a distinct net nearer the gate, and U500 (eight contacts, marked 'FZ' over 'YY', unresolved, beside the crystal Y50 'T327K / EV13' and U43, a five-lead SC70 marked WEJ that TI's SCLS739F addendum gives to the SN74LV1T08 two-input AND gate, extdeps.electronic_component.ti_sn74lv1t08, a candidate) meets that net at one contact (q300_gate_path_reading). U55's pins 16, 15 and 14 (DIR2, DIR1, VCCA under the candidate pinout) each read 500 ohm from Q300's lead b and pin 13 (VCCB) 1200 ohm, the data ports about 1500 ohm: two direction inputs reading what the supply pin reads are tied to VCCA, and a supply rail 500 ohm from the gate is the simplest reading of every front-side 500 ohm point, the gate reaching that rail through a junction, which would make U500's one 500 ohm contact its supply pin rather than a signal. The operator further reports many pads in the unpopulated clusters beside both module receptacles J3 and J4 (U3's neighbourhood on the back below Q300 and Q301, and the like cluster at the other receptacle) reading about 500 ohm from the gate, unnamed (e1_site_clusters_said), and one of them named as a reference, U3's lower-right lead as photographed (U3 a six-lead part marked 'B5' and more, unresolved), 500 ohm: a fourth place the same relationship appears, which is what a rail looks like. Whether the 500 ohm points are a rail or a signal is a powered reading, not yet taken: a rail sits at a steady few volts in every phase, and where the gate's pull-up would come from, if it has one, is then the open question. A crystal beside a candidate AND gate and an eight-contact part, with traces leaving toward the module receptacles, reads more like a qualified timing, reset or sideband distribution than part of the 48 V power path; whether U43's inputs come from Y50 or the board's controls and its output goes to U500 or the receptacles is unread (gate_pin_text) reading lower to Q300's lead b than the return does; its readings join the record once their points are named. Whether U51 reads Q300's node or could drive it is the role of the exact pin the trace meets (register_pin_direction_text), which is unread: a parallel input reads it, a serial output could drive it, a control or clock pin would be shared with whatever clocks the part",
    "TI SNVS950C: the load can be remotely switched off by taking UVLO/EN below its threshold with an open-collector or open-drain device; released, the LM5066I switches on (extdeps.electronic_component.ti_lm5066i vendor statement) -- a mechanism the part admits, not one read on this board",
    "a pasted report, not read against its source: OCP MGX gates a tray's power-on on a management presence and standby handshake (PRSNT, STBY_EN, STBY_RDY). The P4261 is not established as an MGX tray, and no such signal is traced to pin 7",
    "unpowered, the K1's pin 7, read with the probe held on the lead, is reported at 0 ohm to one end of a '200' resistor and not to the ringed via below-right of U1_P5 (hedged: 'seem electrically different'). The K1 is an earlier revision (-100, PCB A01; the E1 -201, PCB B00), so it is a lead about the design, not the E1's network, and it does not separate whether the 2026-10-19 bridge changed the E1's pin 7 network; the bridge was a MOSFET's source to its drain, not on pin 7's network",
    "energized at 48 V, the top end of the part across from pin 21 (reported at 0 ohm to pin 21, read directly, not through the wire, no baseline recorded) read about 4.86 V, hedged ('like 4.86 or something'; first 'it reads 5v'): U1_P5's bias supply reads live at a VDD-like level -- at a point reported at 0 ohm to pin 21, not joined to it by a baseline and not yet separated from pins 20 and 22 -- so on that reading the controller is not off for want of its own supply",
    "the 11-13 mA draw does not establish which circuits are powered, so it neither shows nor excludes other powered logic",
    "U4, the heatsinked device below J4, read 2026-10-21 with its heatsink lifted: Intel's Cyclone 10 GX 10CX085YF672E6G (extdeps.electronic_component.intel_10cx085), an SRAM-based FPGA that loads its configuration at every power-up from a serial flash it masters, a host, or JTAG, and whose user pins, before configuration, pull up or float as its nIO_PULLUP strap selects (the row names the strap rather than the pull-up). The device that would drive Q300's gate is therefore programmable logic whose configuration source and state are unread: the three Micron-format BGAs beside it (K1 listing) are the configuration-flash candidates and the 2 x 5 header below it the JTAG candidate. A gate node at 0 V with 800 ohm to the return is what an unconfigured FPGA's pin, or a configured one holding it low, both look like from outside, so the gate's level does not by itself identify the FPGA's state",
    "U5_2, below U4, read 2026-10-21 with the Microchip logo as CEC1736 (extdeps.electronic_component.microchip_cec1736): a platform root of trust with secure boot, the part NVDebug's debug dumps name beside the FPGA as the ERoT. Three Micron-format BGAs sit beside it (U2_2 and U3_2 'RW188', a third 'RW251'). If U4's configuration flash is one of them and U5_2 guards it, a relation the part's capabilities admit but no reading on this board yet establishes, U4 configures only once U5_2 releases it, and a flash image the root of trust declines, or a root of trust not provisioned on an engineering unit, leaves U4 unconfigured with no switch able to change it. The three flashes decode (Micron's FBGA decoder, 2026-10-21) to two MT25QU01G (U3_2 and U2_2, 1 Gbit each, two die) and one MT25QU02G (2 Gbit, four die), all 1.8 V quad-SPI: a pair of 1 Gbit parts fits a primary and a recovery FPGA image (about 92 Mbit each for this device) and a single 2 Gbit part fits a firmware store, but which image each holds is unread. Energized and settled, DS1_2 beside U5_2 blinks on 1.0 s, off 1.5 s and DS6 beside J68 on 1.36 s, off 1.32 s (two videos, measured frame by frame); two different periods are two different sources, and which part drives each is unread",
    "energized (2026-10-21), at the pads of the three inductors beside U4 against J20's black lead: on the K1 at 40 mA the 2R2 0 V, the 4R7 nearest U4 0 V, the farther 4R7 3.2 V at its pad closer to U4 and 3.0 V at the other; on the E1 settled the nearest 4R7 about 3.2 V and the 2R2 0.94 V (k1_inductor_volts_at_40ma, e1_inductor_volts; the farther 4R7 unread on the E1). Later that day the probe joined the E1's nearest 4R7 to the ground pads under it while energized (e1_inductor_short_incident): the source then cycled CC, 13 mA, 97 mA, CC, and unpowered both of that 4R7's pads read 0 on the 2k range to J20's black lead where the K1's reads about 4 kohm, so that rail is shorted to the return since the incident, a fault on a rail downstream of the enable network, and the E1 is unpowered until it is split at the inductor. Photographed afterward (e1_near_4r7_area_photo), U21 sits directly above the inductor and the silkscreen 'U1_2' at the frame's edge; U21 reads 'P617A / 01 14 / 226' (e1_u21_marking_photo), NXP's PCA9617ADP I2C-bus repeater, as does U53 below it, so U21 is not the inductor's converter and J24 beside them is an I2C / SMBus header candidate; the converter candidate is U100, a 6-lead SOT-23 marked 'C3U / S22 / 25' beside the inductor (e1_u100_photo), its code undecoded. Which loads the rail supplies, the island included, is unread. Read as converter outputs, one of the three inductor outputs recorded is present on the K1 and two are absent where the E1 had all three; whether an absent output is a missing input, an inactive enable, a converter fault or an overloaded load is unread, and the missing 1.8 V at J68 R2 is a fourth absent output of the same standing. On the K1 a momentary bridge across J30's A and B at 40 mA changed neither the current nor the lamps, and S1's pole 2 cycled alone with S2 set as on the E1's P1 left the current where it was (k1_transitions): the logic that answers both on the E1 is in the domain the K1 has not powered",
  ],
  decided_by: "On the K1, unpowered, U100's six pins each to J20's black lead on 2k and to the nearest 4R7's upper pad on the 200 range (the pin at the baseline to each is ground and the switch node), which names the converter's pins without a datasheet; U100's top line re-read under magnification. On the E1, unpowered, J20 disconnected: the affected pad to J20's black lead in diode mode both ways as displayed volts and on the 200 range with the probes reversed, and the K1's same point on the 20k range; the area cleaned and inspected under magnification, underside included. Then, with the converter identified and its switch node, input, enable and power-good named from its datasheet, one of two localizations chosen, not both: the inductor electrically isolated with its solder fully released (no hinged lift) and each side read to J20's black lead, or a controlled low-voltage injection decided only after the rail's backfeed paths and the supply's low-voltage behaviour are known. A component is removed only when a reading names it, and the E1 is not energized until no unexplained low-resistance path remains; the post-repair start is a new phase, never a rewrite of the pre-incident ones. Then the farther 4R7's two pads, and on the K1 the identified converters' input, enable and output at their pins, which separates a missing input from an inactive enable. The E1 is not energized again until the short is located. Then, once repaired and settled, the farther 4R7's two pads against J20's black lead (3.2 and 3.0 V on the K1), and what enables the two converters the K1 holds at 0 V: U9_P2's and U10_P2's enable pins, traced unpowered to the part that drives them, then read energized on both carriers, which names the step the K1 does not take. With the USB Blaster's I/O referenced to R2, a read-only chain scan: the IDCODE, CONF_DONE and nSTATUS, never a configuration, erase or nCONFIG pulse. J24's positions energized in P0, P1 and the settled state against J20's black lead (a position at a steady logic voltage is a supply reference, three that idle high and one that idles low or toggles are the JTAG shape), and unpowered against a baseline to U53, U69 and U21; U4's VCCBAT, read energized at a pad against J20's black lead (its power-on reset holds until it is present). Which part drives DS1_2 and DS6 (U5_2's or U4's pin, traced unpowered), so that each blink names its source; U5_2's release of U4 (its reset or release output to U4's nCONFIG, traced unpowered, then read energized); and the three BGAs' part numbers from Micron's decoder. Energized and settled, CONF_DONE's state (at the FPGA's status LED or a test point once its ball is traced; high reads configured, low unconfigured), which separates a sequencer holding the gate low from one that never loaded; the markings of the three BGAs beside U4 and whether the 2 x 5 header is JTAG (its pins to U4's TCK, TMS, TDI and TDO once traced), through which an unconfigured device reports CONF_DONE directly. Unpowered, first the probes shorted on one recorded range, then on that range: pin 7's own lead to P6, which joins P6 to pin 7 or separates them; the reported zeros re-read so they join or separate (Q301's lone lead to P6, Q301's and Q300's lead a to J20's black lead, Q301's lead b to Q300's lone lead, the resistor's nearer end to lead b, and the via to lead b); Q300's lead b to the exact U51 pin its trace meets, on that range, then that pin's role under SCLS402R (a parallel input reads the node, a serial output could drive it); the resistor's third character confirmed; and whether pin 7 has a pull-up, pin 7's lead to J20's red lead. U51's and U49's markings read 'LV165A' (SN74LV165A, 2026-10-20), so what clocks them is the next part to name. The K38 maker read from a date-code line or another maker's table before any reading names a terminal by the BSS138's pinout. Read (2026-10-20): the pad to J20's black lead 500 ohm with red on the pad and 300 ohm swapped, Q300's lead b to the pad 500 and 1000 ohm, so the paths hold junctions. Then energized at 48 V with all four poles toward ON and settled, against J20's black lead and at pads rather than the UQFN contacts: the lower pad of the part above U500 (the 500 ohm point) and the end of U43's capacitor nearer U43, then the same pad with only S2's poles toward ON; the 500 ohm pad at about 0 V while Q300's lead b reads 0 V says U500's contact holds the node, a few volts there says the 500 ohm path is not a wire. U500's marking read sharply and its dot's corner, then the maker's table. Nothing drives Q300's lead b or pin 7 until a reviewed decision. Later, read-only PMBus status (STATUS_INPUT 7Ch, DIAGNOSTIC_WORD E1h)",
}

// ── THE E1 UNIT (bench readings; design p4261-e1-b) ─────────────────────────────────────────

data e1_design: ElectricalDesignIdentity = "p4261-e1-b" as ElectricalDesignIdentity

data e1_bench: BenchConditions = BenchConditions { power: Unpowered, module: ModuleRemoved }

fn e1_component(local: NonEmptyStr) -> ComponentInstanceIdentity {
  component_instance_identity(design: e1_design, local_identity: local)
}

fn e1_photo(taken_on: NonEmptyStr, locator: NonEmptyStr) -> EvidenceRef {
  OperatorPhotograph { taken_on: taken_on, locator: locator }
}

data e1_j20: ComponentInstanceIdentity = e1_component(local: "J20")

data e1_f1: ComponentInstanceIdentity = e1_component(local: "F1")

data e1_f300: ComponentInstanceIdentity = e1_component(local: "F300")

data e1_f302: ComponentInstanceIdentity = e1_component(local: "F302")

data e1_d2: ComponentInstanceIdentity = e1_component(local: "D2")

data e1_d5: ComponentInstanceIdentity = e1_component(local: "D5")

data e1_c10: ComponentInstanceIdentity = e1_component(local: "C10_P5")

data e1_c12: ComponentInstanceIdentity = e1_component(local: "C12_P5")

data e1_third_can: ComponentInstanceIdentity = e1_component(local: "capacitor below J20 by U522")

data e1_input_fet: ComponentInstanceIdentity = e1_component(local: "input-stage MOSFET probed 2026-10-16 (designator unread)")

data e1_q21: ComponentInstanceIdentity = e1_component(local: "Q21_P5")

data e1_q22: ComponentInstanceIdentity = e1_component(local: "Q22_P5")

data e1_u1_p5: ComponentInstanceIdentity = e1_component(local: "U1_P5")

data e1_bridged_fet: ComponentInstanceIdentity = e1_component(local: "input MOSFET the operator called 'left' (Q21_P5 or Q22_P5, unresolved)")

// J20'S EIGHTEEN POSITIONS. The index runs from the end the operator called pin 1 (2026-10-15, top left
// as photographed, on the row away from the latch); the latch-side row is indexed the same way. Which
// end is the connector maker's pin 1 is unread.
data j20_row_indices: List<Nat> = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9]

fn j20_row_name(side: RowSide) -> String {
  match side {
    LatchSide => "latch-side row"
    AwayFromLatch => "row away from the latch"
    SideUnrecorded => "row of unrecorded side"
  }
}

fn j20_position_terminal(side: RowSide, index: Nat) -> TerminalIdentity {
  (join([j20_row_name(side: side), ", position ", to_string(index)], "") as NonEmptyStr) as TerminalIdentity
}

fn j20_row(side: RowSide) -> List<HousingPosition> {
  map(j20_row_indices, i => HousingPosition { terminal: j20_position_terminal(side: side, index: i), side: side, index: i })
}

data e1_j20_housing: ConnectorHousing = ConnectorHousing {
  component: e1_j20,
  positions: concat(j20_row(side: LatchSide), j20_row(side: AwayFromLatch)),
  sides_evidence: e1_photo(taken_on: "2026-10-16", locator: "J20 photograph annotated RAIL (row by F1 and D2) and GROUND (latch-side row), sent in the session"),
}

fn e1_terminal(c: ComponentInstanceIdentity, name: NonEmptyStr) -> ElectricalTerminalRef {
  terminal_ref(component: c, terminal: name as TerminalIdentity)
}

fn e1_j20_at(side: RowSide, index: Nat) -> ElectricalTerminalRef {
  terminal_ref(component: e1_j20, terminal: j20_position_terminal(side: side, index: index))
}

// The two reference contacts the operator's "power" and "ground" stand for.
data e1_rail_ref: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_j20_at(side: AwayFromLatch, index: 1)

data e1_ground_ref: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_j20_at(side: LatchSide, index: 1)

data e1_f1_near: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_f1, name: "end nearer J20")

data e1_f1_far: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_f1, name: "end farther from J20")

data e1_f300_one: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_f300, name: "one end")

data e1_f300_other: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_f300, name: "other end")

data e1_f302_one: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_f302, name: "one pad")

data e1_f302_other: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_f302, name: "other pad")

data e1_d2_near: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_d2, name: "tab nearer J20")

data e1_d2_far: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_d2, name: "tab farther from J20")

data e1_d5_top: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_d5, name: "top tab")

data e1_d5_bottom: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_d5, name: "bottom tab")

data e1_c10_pos: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_c10, name: "positive")

data e1_c10_neg: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_c10, name: "negative")

data e1_c12_pos: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_c12, name: "positive")

data e1_c12_neg: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_c12, name: "negative")

data e1_fet_terminal_names: List<NonEmptyStr> = ["pin 1", "pin 2", "pin 3", "pin 4", "pin 5", "pin 6", "pin 7", "tab"]

data e1_fet_off_rail: List<NonEmptyStr> = ["pin 1", "pin 2", "pin 3", "pin 5", "pin 6", "pin 7"]

// THE INFERENCES. "Ground" in the operator's readings is J20's latch-side row: they named that row ground
// first (2026-10-15, "the entire bottom row is ground"), and the annotated photograph puts it on the latch
// side. "Power" / "rail" is the row away from the latch, the nine positions read to both ends of F1. Which
// point of each row the probe touched is unrecorded; position 1 stands for it.
data e1_ground_basis: NonEmptyStr = "the operator's 'ground' is J20's latch-side row (2026-10-15 'the entire bottom row is ground'; the annotated photograph's GROUND row); the point on it is unrecorded and position 1 stands for it"

data e1_rail_basis: NonEmptyStr = "the operator's 'power' / 'rail' is J20's fused row away from the latch (2026-10-15 'all 9 on top are joined to the fuse'; the annotated photograph's RAIL row); the point on it is unrecorded and position 1 stands for it"

data e1_row_basis: NonEmptyStr = "'the entire bottom row is ground': each latch-side position beeps to the operator's ground reference, taken as the same row's position 1"

// POPULATION STATEMENTS NAME NO EXACT FIRST POINT. "Everything I touched", "only the big tab and the very
// middle pin" and "nothing seems to be connected to ground" cover visible terminals without saying which
// were probed; each terminal the statement covers stands for a touch, inferred with that basis.
data e1_touched_basis: NonEmptyStr = "'everything i touched had continuity to power' (F300, F302): which points were touched is unrecorded; the named parts' two visible terminals each stand for a touch"

data e1_middle_pin_basis: NonEmptyStr = "'the very middle little small pin': the middle of the MOSFET's seven leads, which the IPB017N10N5LF pinout numbers pin 4; the number is read off the lead geometry, not off the board"

data e1_only_basis: NonEmptyStr = "'only the BIG tab and the very middle little small pin are connected to rail power': whether each other lead was touched is unrecorded; 'only' is taken to cover every visible lead"

data e1_nothing_basis: NonEmptyStr = "'nothing seems to be connected to ground': whether each lead and the tab were touched is unrecorded; 'nothing' is taken to cover every visible terminal"

fn touched_to(a: ElectricalTerminalRef, reference: ElectricalTerminalRef, first_basis: NonEmptyStr, second_basis: NonEmptyStr, result: ContinuityResult, evidence: EvidenceRef) -> ContinuityObservation {
  e1_read(a: a, b: reference, record: both_points_inferred(first_basis: first_basis, second_basis: second_basis), result: result, evidence: evidence)
}

fn e1_read(a: ElectricalTerminalRef, b: ElectricalTerminalRef, record: ProbeRecord, result: ContinuityResult, evidence: EvidenceRef) -> ContinuityObservation {
  ContinuityObservation { asset: p4261_e1_b, first: a, second: b, record: record, conditions: e1_bench, result: result, evidence: evidence }
}

fn to_ground(a: ElectricalTerminalRef, result: ContinuityResult, evidence: EvidenceRef) -> ContinuityObservation {
  e1_read(a: a, b: e1_ground_ref, record: second_point_inferred(basis: e1_ground_basis), result: result, evidence: evidence)
}

fn to_rail(a: ElectricalTerminalRef, result: ContinuityResult, evidence: EvidenceRef) -> ContinuityObservation {
  e1_read(a: a, b: e1_rail_ref, record: second_point_inferred(basis: e1_rail_basis), result: result, evidence: evidence)
}

data e1_fuse_ends_said: EvidenceRef = OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-15", verbatim: "regarding the 'which end of the fuse' the 9 supply pins beep to both ends of the fuse" }

data e1_bottom_row_said: EvidenceRef = OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-15", verbatim: "the entire bottom row is ground" }

data e1_d2_tabs_said: EvidenceRef = OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-15", verbatim: "regarding the tabs - D2 closer to J20 is connected to power, the farther tab is connected to ground (near the grounded cap terminals)" }

data e1_caps_said: EvidenceRef = OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-15", verbatim: "J20 supply did not seem to connect to the caps like that" }

data e1_d5_tabs_said: EvidenceRef = OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-16", verbatim: "the top of D5 is connected to ground, the bottom is connected to power rail and everything else" }

data e1_fuses_said: EvidenceRef = OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-16", verbatim: "F200 seems to be connected mostly to the rail, not ground, same with F302 - everything i touched had continuity to power / yeah F300 mb" }

data e1_fet_said: EvidenceRef = OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-16", verbatim: "only the BIG tab and the very middle little small  pin are conneted to rail power, nothing seems to be connected to ground" }

fn fet_terminal(name: NonEmptyStr) -> ElectricalTerminalRef {
  e1_terminal(c: e1_input_fet, name: name)
}

// THE ENERGIZED READING (2026-10-18). The Jesverty SPS-6005V fed J20 through two bare-wire leads, red in a
// cavity of the row away from the latch and black in a latch-side cavity, which cavities unrecorded, so
// each lead's point is inferred onto its row's position 1 as the continuity readings' are. The limit was
// set to 0.10 A on shorted leads with over-current shutoff armed; the operator stepped the voltage to
// 52 V and the shutoff did not trip. The draw is the display at 52 V; the open reading is the same
// setting with the board disconnected. No per-step table was recorded.
data e1_energized_bench: BenchConditions = BenchConditions { power: Energized, module: ModuleRemoved }

data e1_red_lead_basis: NonEmptyStr = "the red lead sat in a J20 cavity of the row away from the latch (2026-10-18 'put a red/black wire in ground/rail of the j20 slot'); which cavity is unrecorded and position 1 stands for it"

data e1_black_lead_basis: NonEmptyStr = "the black lead sat in a latch-side J20 cavity; which cavity is unrecorded and position 1 stands for it"

data e1_j20_draw: SourceDrawObservation = SourceDrawObservation {
  asset: p4261_e1_b,
  feed: e1_rail_ref,
  return_terminal: e1_ground_ref,
  leads: both_points_inferred(first_basis: e1_red_lead_basis, second_basis: e1_black_lead_basis),
  conditions: e1_energized_bench,
  setting: SourceSetting { voltage: volt(count: 52), current_limit: milliampere(count: 100), protection: OverCurrentShutoffArmed },
  open_reading: milliampere(count: 0),
  loaded_reading: milliampere(count: 13),
  stepping_peak: Present { value: milliampere(count: 20) },
  behaviour: HeldBelowLimit,
  evidence: [
    OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-18", verbatim: "its fine, its sitting at 52v, .013A, .675W / it mostly sat at .011A as power in creased" },
    OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-18", verbatim: "when i was raising the voltage it would go to like 20ma, but then immediately back down" },
    OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-18", verbatim: "it showed .000 with nothing connected, and then jumped immediately back to .013A when i reconnected it" },
  ],
}

// THE INPUT SWITCHES READ LIVE (2026-10-19). J20 at 48 V through the same leads, module removed, the
// meter's black probe on the supply's negative terminal, which the black lead joins to J20's latch-side
// row. The operator read each input MOSFET's tab and its small leads: "both mosfets are getting 48v on
// their input and the small output legs all read 1v". Which small leads were touched is unrecorded, so
// each of the six stands for a touch. During the same session one MOSFET's lead positions 3 and 4 were
// bridged with a pop; whether these readings came before or after it is unrecorded.
data e1_live_bench: BenchConditions = BenchConditions { power: Energized, module: ModuleRemoved }

data e1_supply_return_basis: NonEmptyStr = "the meter's black probe sat on the bench supply's negative terminal, which the black lead joins to J20's latch-side row; position 1 stands for the row"

data e1_small_legs_basis: NonEmptyStr = "'the small output legs all read 1v': which of the six small leads were touched is unrecorded, so each stands for a touch"

data e1_input_tab_basis: NonEmptyStr = "'getting 48v on their input': the wide tab on the board-edge side, which the operator was asked to read as the input"

data e1_switch_said: EvidenceRef = OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: "ok basically what i'm seeing is that both mosfets are getting 48v on their input and the small output legs all read 1v, the ground leg reads 48v" }

data e1_small_leg_names: List<NonEmptyStr> = ["pin 1", "pin 2", "pin 3", "pin 5", "pin 6", "pin 7"]

data e1_bridge_incident: BenchIncident = BenchIncident {
  key: "2026-10-19 probe bridge",
  asset: p4261_e1_b,
  bridged: [e1_terminal(c: e1_bridged_fet, name: "lead position 3 from the operator's left"), e1_terminal(c: e1_bridged_fet, name: "lead position 4 from the operator's left (the drain stub)")],
  record: both_points_inferred(first_basis: "'the 3rd and fourth leg from the left [1, 2, 3, 4, ...]': position 3 is pin 3 or pin 5 by the package's numbering direction, unread", second_basis: "position 4 of seven is the middle lead, pin 4, the drain stub, whichever way the leads are numbered"),
  conditions: e1_live_bench,
  observed: "an audible pop while energized at 48 V",
  inspection: NoDamageSeen { looked_at: "top and bottom of the board, by eye (2026-10-19 'i don't see any physical damage to the board on the top or bottom')" },
  evidence: OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: "when touching the mosfets i accidentally shorted one leg of the mosfet to the ground leg a sec and saw a pop / i'm pretty sure it was the left transistor / the 3rd and fourth leg from the left [1, 2, 3, 4, ...] with 4 being ground i guess" },
}

fn e1_switch_reading(c: ComponentInstanceIdentity, terminal: NonEmptyStr, first_basis: NonEmptyStr, millivolts: Nat) -> NodeVoltageObservation {
  NodeVoltageObservation {
    asset: p4261_e1_b,
    at: e1_terminal(c: c, name: terminal),
    reference: e1_ground_ref,
    record: both_points_inferred(first_basis: first_basis, second_basis: e1_supply_return_basis),
    conditions: e1_live_bench,
    source: volt(count: 48),
    value: ReadAbout { value: millivolt(count: millivolts) },
    certainty: StatedPlainly,
    order: OrderUnrecorded { relative_to: [e1_bridge_incident.key] },
    evidence: [e1_switch_said],
  }
}

fn e1_switch_readings(c: ComponentInstanceIdentity) -> List<NodeVoltageObservation> {
  concat([e1_switch_reading(c: c, terminal: "tab", first_basis: e1_input_tab_basis, millivolts: 48000)], map(e1_small_leg_names, n => e1_switch_reading(c: c, terminal: n, first_basis: e1_small_legs_basis, millivolts: 1000)))
}

// U1_P5'S OVERVOLTAGE PAD (2026-10-19, all after the probe bridge). Pins 7 to 10 each end in a covered
// via beside the lead. On the back, a via pad beside the '01B' resistor first read near zero to
// "pin 7" with the probe touching pins 7 and 8 together; read with the probe held to one lead, it is
// reported on pin 8 ("i can show its pin 8", no display or baseline recorded) and separated from pins 7
// and 9, so the operator reads it as OVLO's; no baseline reading joins it to pin 8. That first join is not
// recorded: it was a reading of two leads at once. Unpowered, with the supply's leads unplugged, from
// that pad: the ground ring (itself on J20's return), Q5_P5's single lead (on the return), D5_P5's
// nearer end, the '01B' resistor's ends and Q21_P5's tab. Energized through the same leads, the pad
// read at two source settings.
data e1_ovlo_pad: ComponentInstanceIdentity = e1_component(local: "back-side via pad beside the 01B resistor, behind U1_P5")

data e1_ground_ring: ComponentInstanceIdentity = e1_component(local: "copper mounting ring behind U3_P5 (back side)")

data e1_01b: ComponentInstanceIdentity = e1_component(local: "01B resistor below D5_P5 (back side)")

data e1_back_photo: EvidenceRef = e1_photo(taken_on: "2026-10-19", locator: "https://drive.google.com/open?id=1dENn7_kYwOHHLdflkGU4gxcwa-cmTh2r (back side behind U1_P5, the pin 7 pad arrowed)")

data e1_u1_closeup_photo: EvidenceRef = e1_photo(taken_on: "2026-10-19", locator: "https://drive.google.com/open?id=1xNIV61IHgIy_s8mNq_z1D9KYJaciscui (U1_P5 close-up, the pin 1 triangle at the top left)")

data e1_twenty_k_hedge: StatementCertainty = StatedHedged { verbatim: "i think 20kohm yeah" }

data e1_return_basis: NonEmptyStr = "'ground' is J20's latch-side row; position 1 stands for it"

fn e1_pad_ohms(to: ElectricalTerminalRef, display: ResistanceDisplay, range: MeterRange, certainty: StatementCertainty, said: NonEmptyStr) -> ResistanceObservation {
  ResistanceObservation {
    asset: p4261_e1_b, first: e1_terminal(c: e1_ovlo_pad, name: "pad"), second: to, record: both_points_recorded, conditions: e1_bench, polarity: PolarityUnrecorded,
    range: range, display: display, stability: StabilityUnrecorded, certainty: certainty, order: AfterIncidents { keys: [e1_bridge_incident.key] },
    evidence: [OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: said }, e1_back_photo],
  }
}

fn e1_to_return(from: ElectricalTerminalRef, said: NonEmptyStr) -> ResistanceObservation {
  ResistanceObservation {
    asset: p4261_e1_b, first: from, second: e1_ground_ref, record: second_point_inferred(basis: e1_return_basis), conditions: e1_bench, polarity: PolarityUnrecorded,
    range: RangeUnrecorded, display: DisplayZeroWithoutBaseline { reported: "ground" }, stability: StabilityUnrecorded, certainty: StatedPlainly, order: AfterIncidents { keys: [e1_bridge_incident.key] },
    evidence: [OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: said }, e1_back_photo],
  }
}

fn e1_pad_to_pin(pin: NonEmptyStr, display: ResistanceDisplay, said: NonEmptyStr) -> ResistanceObservation {
  ResistanceObservation {
    asset: p4261_e1_b, first: e1_terminal(c: e1_ovlo_pad, name: "pad"), second: e1_terminal(c: e1_u1_p5, name: pin), record: both_points_recorded, conditions: e1_bench, polarity: PolarityUnrecorded,
    range: RangeUnrecorded, display: display, stability: StabilityUnrecorded, certainty: StatedPlainly, order: AfterIncidents { keys: [e1_bridge_incident.key] },
    evidence: [OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: said }, e1_back_photo, e1_u1_closeup_photo],
  }
}

data e1_ovlo_pad_resistances: List<ResistanceObservation> = [
  e1_pad_to_pin(pin: "pin 8", display: DisplayZeroWithoutBaseline { reported: "its pin 8" }, said: "the pad is OVLO, not pin 7, the problem is when imeasure it from the other side i have to hold the probe at both pin 7 and 8, but when i'm careful and holding tape to the pad i can show its pin 8"),
  e1_pad_to_pin(pin: "pin 7", display: DisplayAboveBaseline, said: "yeah its separate from pin 7 and 9"),
  e1_pad_to_pin(pin: "pin 9", display: DisplayAboveBaseline, said: "yeah its separate from pin 7 and 9"),
  e1_pad_ohms(to: e1_terminal(c: e1_ground_ring, name: "ring"), display: DisplayValue { ohms: 3500, approximate: false }, range: RangeFullScale { ohms: 20000 }, certainty: e1_twenty_k_hedge, said: "to a ground copper ring is 3500ohm / i think 20kohm yeah"),
  e1_to_return(from: e1_terminal(c: e1_ground_ring, name: "ring"), said: "yes the copper rings are ground"),
  e1_to_return(from: e1_terminal(c: e1_component(local: "Q5_P5"), name: "single lead"), said: "the q5_p5 leg is ground"),
  e1_pad_ohms(to: e1_terminal(c: e1_component(local: "D5_P5"), name: "end nearer the OVLO (pin 8) pad"), display: DisplayValue { ohms: 5000, approximate: false }, range: RangeFullScale { ohms: 20000 }, certainty: e1_twenty_k_hedge, said: "5kohm to the near side of d5_p5"),
  e1_pad_ohms(to: e1_terminal(c: e1_component(local: "Q5_P5"), name: "single lead"), display: DisplayValue { ohms: 3500, approximate: false }, range: RangeFullScale { ohms: 20000 }, certainty: e1_twenty_k_hedge, said: "3500ohm to one of the three legs (the lone one)"),
  e1_pad_ohms(to: e1_terminal(c: e1_01b, name: "one end"), display: DisplayOverRange, range: RangeUnrecorded, certainty: StatedPlainly, said: "01b don't see anything"),
  e1_pad_ohms(to: e1_terminal(c: e1_01b, name: "other end"), display: DisplayOverRange, range: RangeUnrecorded, certainty: StatedPlainly, said: "01b don't see anything"),
  e1_pad_ohms(to: e1_terminal(c: e1_q21, name: "tab"), display: DisplayValue { ohms: 500000, approximate: true }, range: RangeFullScale { ohms: 2000000 }, certainty: StatedHedged { verbatim: "it showed .5 or something at 2mohm" }, said: "the q21 tab at 2mohm shows like a lot of resistance / it showed .5 or something at 2mohm"),
]

fn e1_pad_volts(source_volts: Nat, millivolts: Nat, said: NonEmptyStr) -> NodeVoltageObservation {
  NodeVoltageObservation {
    asset: p4261_e1_b, at: e1_terminal(c: e1_ovlo_pad, name: "pad"), reference: e1_ground_ref, record: second_point_inferred(basis: e1_supply_return_basis),
    conditions: e1_live_bench, source: volt(count: source_volts), value: ReadAbout { value: millivolt(count: millivolts) }, certainty: StatedPlainly,
    order: AfterIncidents { keys: [e1_bridge_incident.key] }, evidence: [OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: said }, e1_back_photo],
  }
}

// THE WIRE MEANT FOR PIN 7 IS ITS OWN POINT (2026-10-19, after the probe bridge). The operator taped a
// thin wire where they took U1_P5 pin 7 to be and took every later "pin 7" reading at it, until they
// doubted where it sat. What the meter touched was the wire, so each of those readings is recorded at
// the wire's point, and e1_pin7_attachment says only that it was meant for pin 7: no reading joins the
// wire to pin 7's lead at the shorted-probe baseline, so none of its readings stands for pin 7. The
// readings do place the wire: not at the baseline to pin 8's pad; about 500 ohm to a back-side pad on
// the ground rings, with the wire on the meter's COM probe (with the probes swapped it reads
// differently, below); 16 kohm to pin 21 (VDD), so not joined to VDD when that was read; kilohms to
// Q21_P5's tab, so not on the 48 V side. Energized, the wire held about 1.0 V with the source at 36, 48
// and 54 V. Readings taken before the wire, with the probe held on the lead, stay at pin 7 itself
// (e1_ovlo_pad_resistances). The K1's pin 7 was read later without a wire (k1_resistances): an earlier
// revision's network, it does not separate whether the probe bridge changed the E1's -- the bridge
// itself was a MOSFET's source to its drain, not on pin 7's network.
//
// The disputes are the operator's: "pin 7 also says 5v", then "pin 7 seems to read 0v, it may have
// bridged to pin 21 - pin 8 reads ~1.6v", and that pin 7 may never have read 1 V. They were said in a
// session turn lost to a usage limit and reach the record through the operator's later paste quoting
// them; the source setting and the point each was read at are unrecorded, so they are disputes of the
// attachment, not voltage readings.
data e1_ground_pad: ComponentInstanceIdentity = e1_component(local: "back-side pad first read from the pin 7 wire, on the ground rings")

data e1_pin7_wire_said: NonEmptyStr = "I taped a thin wire to pin 7 now so I can explore the bottom"

data e1_pin7_wire: ComponentInstanceIdentity = e1_component(local: "taped wire meant for U1_P5 pin 7")

data e1_pin7_wire_end: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_pin7_wire, name: "(free end)")

data e1_pin7_attachment: ProbeAttachment = ProbeAttachment {
  point: e1_pin7_wire_end,
  intended: e1_terminal(c: e1_u1_p5, name: "pin 7"),
  statement: OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: e1_pin7_wire_said },
  disputes: [
    OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: "now i see pin 7 also says 5v? Am i confused?" },
    OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: "oh, pin 7 seems to read 0v, it may have bridged to pin 21 - pin 8 reads ~1.6v - i forgot we were confusing them earlier - i'm not sure we ever observed pin 7 reading 1v, maybe you could confirm" },
  ],
  ruling: [],
}

// placed: the statements naming which probe touched the wire, when the reading's own words do not.
fn e1_wire_read(to: ElectricalTerminalRef, record: ProbeRecord, polarity: ProbePolarity, placed: List<EvidenceRef>, range: MeterRange, display: ResistanceDisplay, certainty: StatementCertainty, said: NonEmptyStr) -> ResistanceObservation {
  ResistanceObservation {
    asset: p4261_e1_b, first: e1_pin7_wire_end, second: to, record: record, conditions: e1_bench, polarity: polarity,
    range: range, display: display, stability: StabilityUnrecorded, certainty: certainty, order: AfterIncidents { keys: [e1_bridge_incident.key] },
    evidence: concat([OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: said }, OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: e1_pin7_wire_said }, e1_u1_closeup_photo], placed),
  }
}

// The wire on the meter's COM (black) probe, so the red probe on the other point: the operator's
// statement for the readings from the wire ("pin 7") to the parts on the back.
data e1_wire_on_com: List<EvidenceRef> = [OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: "sorry - so to be clear, the 500 to the parts on the back were done in the \"wrong\" direction, with pin 7 on the ground port of the multimeter" }]

data e1_wire_resistances: List<ResistanceObservation> = [
  e1_wire_read(to: e1_terminal(c: e1_ovlo_pad, name: "pad"), record: both_points_recorded, polarity: PolarityUnrecorded, placed: [], range: RangeUnrecorded, display: DisplayAboveBaseline, certainty: StatedPlainly, said: "Yeah it's not on pin 8, I checked"),
  e1_wire_read(to: e1_terminal(c: e1_ground_pad, name: "pad"), record: both_points_recorded, polarity: RedOnSecond, placed: e1_wire_on_com, range: RangeUnrecorded, display: DisplayValue { ohms: 500, approximate: false }, certainty: StatedPlainly, said: "This pad is 500 ohms to pin 7"),
  e1_to_return(from: e1_terminal(c: e1_ground_pad, name: "pad"), said: "I think that pad is ground., it's the same as copper rings"),
]

// THE LATER READINGS FROM THE WIRE, every one with the supply's leads unplugged. Each is kept as read,
// and none is reconciled with another: a reading that disagrees with an earlier one of the same pair is
// a second link, not a correction.
//
// Q300's, Q301's and a small resistor's points read 700 ohm from the wire, then 550 ohm with ground
// ("Not sure what changed"), all with the wire on the meter's COM probe. Which lead of each transistor,
// and which resistor, is unrecorded, so each is named as read rather than stood in by a lead it may
// not be; four points reading the same value from the wire are four links, not one node. Pin 21 and
// Q21_P5's tab were read with the probes' placement unstated, which stays unrecorded.
//
// The wire to the ground pad depends on which probe touched which point: 557 ohm on the 2k range with
// the red probe on the pad, over range on the 2k range and about 11 kohm on the 20k range with the red
// probe on the wire. Which probe this meter drives positive in resistance mode is unverified, so the
// readings say which probe touched which point and nothing about which way a junction conducts.
data e1_q300_leg: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_component(local: "Q300"), name: "leg read from the pin 7 wire (which of the three unrecorded)")

data e1_q301_leg: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_component(local: "Q301"), name: "leg read from the pin 7 wire (which of the three unrecorded)")

data e1_small_resistor_pad: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_component(local: "small resistor near Q300 / Q301 (which one unrecorded)"), name: "pad read from the pin 7 wire")

data e1_shared_700_said: NonEmptyStr = "One leg of each q300 and q301 share 700ohms with pin 7, and one of the small resistors shares one pad of 700ohm"

data e1_shared_550_said: NonEmptyStr = "Now it's reading 550 ohms on all of them and ground / Not sure what changed"

data e1_them_basis: NonEmptyStr = "'on all of them': the three points that read 700 ohm from the wire just before"

data e1_and_ground_basis: NonEmptyStr = "'and ground': which ground point is unrecorded; J20's latch-side row position 1 stands for it"

data e1_pin21_basis: NonEmptyStr = "'That reads 16k': the point asked for from the wire, U1_P5 pin 21 (VDD), the seventh lead up the right-hand column; the operator did not name it, nor the range"

data e1_q21_tab_basis: NonEmptyStr = "'on 200k it reads 40, on 2m it reads .100': the point asked for, Q21_P5's wide tab; the operator named the ranges, not the point"

data e1_q21_tab_said: NonEmptyStr = "on 200k it reads \"40\", on 2m it reads \".100\" - not sure if that makes sense."

data e1_q21_tab_hedge: StatementCertainty = StatedHedged { verbatim: "not sure if that makes sense" }

data e1_ground_pad_basis: NonEmptyStr = "'red is on ground': the point asked for, the back-side ground pad that read 500 ohm from the wire"

data e1_red_on_pad_said: NonEmptyStr = "its 557 / sorry - black is on pin 7, and red is on ground for 557"

data e1_red_on_pin7_said: NonEmptyStr = "that doesn't read at 2k, it reads 11 at 20k"

data e1_wire_later_resistances: List<ResistanceObservation> = concat(concat(
  map([e1_q300_leg, e1_q301_leg, e1_small_resistor_pad], t => e1_wire_read(to: t, record: both_points_recorded, polarity: RedOnSecond, placed: e1_wire_on_com, range: RangeUnrecorded, display: DisplayValue { ohms: 700, approximate: false }, certainty: StatedPlainly, said: e1_shared_700_said)),
  map([e1_q300_leg, e1_q301_leg, e1_small_resistor_pad], t => e1_wire_read(to: t, record: second_point_inferred(basis: e1_them_basis), polarity: RedOnSecond, placed: e1_wire_on_com, range: RangeUnrecorded, display: DisplayValue { ohms: 550, approximate: false }, certainty: StatedPlainly, said: e1_shared_550_said))),
  [
    e1_wire_read(to: e1_ground_ref, record: second_point_inferred(basis: e1_and_ground_basis), polarity: RedOnSecond, placed: e1_wire_on_com, range: RangeUnrecorded, display: DisplayValue { ohms: 550, approximate: false }, certainty: StatedPlainly, said: e1_shared_550_said),
    e1_wire_read(to: e1_terminal(c: e1_u1_p5, name: "pin 21"), record: second_point_inferred(basis: e1_pin21_basis), polarity: PolarityUnrecorded, placed: [], range: RangeUnrecorded, display: DisplayValue { ohms: 16000, approximate: false }, certainty: StatedPlainly, said: "That reads 16k"),
    e1_wire_read(to: e1_terminal(c: e1_q21, name: "tab"), record: second_point_inferred(basis: e1_q21_tab_basis), polarity: PolarityUnrecorded, placed: [], range: RangeFullScale { ohms: 200000 }, display: DisplayValue { ohms: 40000, approximate: true }, certainty: e1_q21_tab_hedge, said: e1_q21_tab_said),
    e1_wire_read(to: e1_terminal(c: e1_q21, name: "tab"), record: second_point_inferred(basis: e1_q21_tab_basis), polarity: PolarityUnrecorded, placed: [], range: RangeFullScale { ohms: 2000000 }, display: DisplayValue { ohms: 100000, approximate: true }, certainty: e1_q21_tab_hedge, said: e1_q21_tab_said),
    e1_wire_read(to: e1_terminal(c: e1_ground_pad, name: "pad"), record: second_point_inferred(basis: e1_ground_pad_basis), polarity: RedOnSecond, placed: [], range: RangeFullScale { ohms: 2000 }, display: DisplayValue { ohms: 557, approximate: false }, certainty: StatedPlainly, said: e1_red_on_pad_said),
    e1_wire_read(to: e1_terminal(c: e1_ground_pad, name: "pad"), record: second_point_inferred(basis: e1_ground_pad_basis), polarity: RedOnFirst, placed: [], range: RangeFullScale { ohms: 2000 }, display: DisplayOverRange, certainty: StatedPlainly, said: e1_red_on_pin7_said),
    e1_wire_read(to: e1_terminal(c: e1_ground_pad, name: "pad"), record: second_point_inferred(basis: e1_ground_pad_basis), polarity: RedOnFirst, placed: [], range: RangeFullScale { ohms: 20000 }, display: DisplayValue { ohms: 11000, approximate: true }, certainty: StatedPlainly, said: e1_red_on_pin7_said),
  ])

// PIN 21'S PART AND VDD (2026-10-19, after the probe bridge), probed directly on pin 21, not through the
// taped wire. Pin 21 (VDD) is reported at 0 ohm to the top end of a beige two-terminal part directly
// across (no baseline recorded), with a visible trace, as on the K1; the boards' parts there are each their own. Readings taken
// from the taped wire after the K1's (the ringed via, the resistor in the K1's '200' position) are not
// recorded yet.
//
// Energized at 48 V, that top end read about 4.86 V against J20's return -- first "5v", then, asked for
// the digits, "like 4.86 or something": one reading, refined, and hedged. It says the node is live at a
// bias-supply level, far from 0 V and from the input. That it is VDD rests on the baseline join to pin
// 21 and the trace, but no reading separates that top end from pins 20 and 22, so by the access-point
// rule it is not yet pin 21's access point (and SNVS950C lets CL and ADR0 be tied to VDD, so for this
// pin that rule cannot be met by every board); no standing reads the pin's window from it.
data e1_beige: ComponentInstanceIdentity = e1_component(local: "beige two-terminal part directly across from U1_P5 pin 21")

data e1_beige_top: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_beige, name: "top end")

data e1_pin21_resistances: List<ResistanceObservation> = [
  ResistanceObservation {
    asset: p4261_e1_b, first: e1_terminal(c: e1_u1_p5, name: "pin 21"), second: e1_beige_top,
    record: both_points_inferred(first_basis: "'it reads 0 on both boards': the point asked for on the E1, U1_P5 pin 21, the eighth lead down the right-hand column, as on the K1", second_basis: "the point asked for, the top end of the beige part directly across from pin 21"),
    conditions: e1_bench, polarity: PolarityUnrecorded, range: RangeUnrecorded, display: DisplayZeroWithoutBaseline { reported: "0" }, stability: StabilityUnrecorded, certainty: StatedPlainly,
    order: AfterIncidents { keys: [e1_bridge_incident.key] }, evidence: [OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: "yes, it reads 0 on both boards, and the trace is clearly visible on both" }],
  },
]

data e1_vdd_volts: NodeVoltageObservation = NodeVoltageObservation {
  asset: p4261_e1_b, at: e1_beige_top, reference: e1_ground_ref,
  record: both_points_inferred(first_basis: "'it reads 5v', then 'yes its like 4.86 or something': the point asked for, the top end of the beige part across from pin 21 (reported at 0 ohm to pin 21), on the DC 20 V range asked for", second_basis: "the meter's black probe on J20's black lead, which joins J20's latch-side row; position 1 stands for the row"),
  conditions: e1_live_bench, source: volt(count: 48), value: ReadAbout { value: millivolt(count: 4860) }, certainty: StatedHedged { verbatim: "like 4.86 or something" },
  order: AfterIncidents { keys: [e1_bridge_incident.key] },
  evidence: [OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: "it reads 5v" }, OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: "yes its like 4.86 or something" }],
}

fn e1_wire_volts(source_volts: Nat) -> NodeVoltageObservation {
  NodeVoltageObservation {
    asset: p4261_e1_b, at: e1_pin7_wire_end, reference: e1_ground_ref, record: second_point_inferred(basis: e1_supply_return_basis),
    conditions: e1_live_bench, source: volt(count: source_volts), value: ReadAbout { value: millivolt(count: 1000) }, certainty: StatedPlainly,
    order: AfterIncidents { keys: [e1_bridge_incident.key] },
    evidence: [OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: "It's steady at 1v always / It was 36v, 48v, and 54v I tried" }, OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: e1_pin7_wire_said }],
  }
}

// RP1 AND THE SECOND WIRE (2026-10-19, the operator's next session; after the probe bridge). RP1 is the
// round pad with a white silkscreen ring right of U1_P5, named for where it is, not for a signal. The
// first wire read near zero to it ("on the E1, its the circle you pointed to"), with no baseline
// recorded, so the wire and RP1 stay two measured nodes. With no wire on the chip and the probe held on pin 7's own lead, RP1 read
// about 1.3 kohm -- the lowest the operator found from that lead in the controller's neighbourhood -- so
// RP1 is not pin 7's access point and no point near pin 7 is. The operator's "seems like pin 21" for RP1
// is not a reading: none joins RP1 to pin 21. The 1.3 kohm display's range is unrecorded; a 200 ohm
// range cannot show it.
//
// A second wire, W2 (the stranded red conductor of a red/black pair), was taped at the middle of the
// left-hand row. With the meter's red probe on J20's black lead and black on its far end it read over
// range on the 2k range; the operator found it was not touching pin 7, reseated it, and closed the
// attempt because it kept moving. Asked about the first wire's disputes, the operator does not remember
// the setting or probe point of the 0 V, 1.6 V and 5 V reports, and thinks the supply's current did not
// change at the 5 V report ("i don't think so though").
data e1_rp1: ComponentInstanceIdentity = e1_component(local: "RP1: round pad with a white silkscreen ring, right of U1_P5")

data e1_rp1_pad: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_rp1, name: "pad")

data e1_rp1_photo: EvidenceRef = e1_photo(taken_on: "2026-10-19", locator: "bench-session upload c8eee6bb, U1_P5 with the second wire; RP1 circled in the reply (not on Drive)")

data e1_rp1_resistances: List<ResistanceObservation> = [
  e1_wire_read(to: e1_rp1_pad, record: second_point_inferred(basis: "'its the circle you pointed to': the ringed point asked about, which the wire read near zero to"), polarity: PolarityUnrecorded, placed: [], range: RangeUnrecorded, display: DisplayZeroWithoutBaseline { reported: "its the circle you pointed to" }, certainty: StatedPlainly, said: "the two boards seem electrically different here: on the E1, its the circle you pointed to"),
  ResistanceObservation {
    asset: p4261_e1_b, first: e1_terminal(c: e1_u1_p5, name: "pin 7"), second: e1_rp1_pad,
    record: second_point_inferred(basis: "'that ringed wire': the ringed point RP1, the point just asked about"),
    conditions: e1_bench, polarity: PolarityUnrecorded, range: RangeUnrecorded, display: DisplayValue { ohms: 1300, approximate: true }, stability: StabilityUnrecorded, certainty: StatedPlainly,
    order: AfterIncidents { keys: [e1_bridge_incident.key] },
    evidence: [
      OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: "that ringed wire reads 1.3k directly to pin 7" },
      OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: "in that area, the closest i could find was 1.3k to basically what seems like pin 21 (that circled test pad) or whatever the circle connects to" },
      e1_rp1_photo,
    ],
  },
]

data e1_w2: ComponentInstanceIdentity = e1_component(local: "W2: stranded red conductor of a red/black pair, taped at U1_P5's left-hand row")

data e1_w2_end: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_w2, name: "(far end)")

data e1_w2_attachment: ProbeAttachment = ProbeAttachment {
  point: e1_w2_end,
  intended: e1_terminal(c: e1_u1_p5, name: "pin 7"),
  statement: OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: "It should be better now" },
  disputes: [
    OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: "OK - the wire was not making contact with pin 7, but it is now" },
    OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: "sorry - the wire thing is not working (sad face) it keeps moving etc" },
  ],
  ruling: [],
}

data e1_w2_resistances: List<ResistanceObservation> = [
  ResistanceObservation {
    asset: p4261_e1_b, first: e1_w2_end, second: e1_ground_ref,
    record: both_points_inferred(first_basis: "the sheet's M4: the meter's black probe on the red wire's far end", second_basis: "the sheet's M4: the red probe on J20's black lead, which joins J20's latch-side row; position 1 stands for the row"),
    conditions: e1_bench, polarity: RedOnSecond, range: RangeFullScale { ohms: 2000 }, display: DisplayOverRange, stability: StabilityUnrecorded, certainty: StatedPlainly,
    order: AfterIncidents { keys: [e1_bridge_incident.key] },
    evidence: [OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: "Sorry - M4 - returned no contact for this, does that make sense?" }],
  },
]

// THE LEADS READ DIRECTLY (2026-10-19, the operator's next session; after the probe bridge). With
// nothing wired to the chip, the operator held the red probe on U1_P5's leads, the black probe on J20's
// black lead, the source at 48 V with the 0.1 A limit and the module removed: pin 8 about 1.8 V -- what
// its back-side pad read at 48 V, so the count from the pin 1 marker holds -- and pin 7 0 V. A probe
// touching nothing also reads 0 V; pin 8 read the same way just before. Unpowered, pin 7's lead to J20's
// black lead reads over range on the 200 ohm range both ways; about 535 ohm with the red probe on J20's
// lead; over range on the 2k range and about 11 kohm on the 20k range with the red probe on pin 7 --
// the pattern the first wire read to the ground pad, which is consistent with that wire having been on
// pin 7 then, and is still no join of it. A close photograph of the left-hand row shows no solder bridge
// between leads 1 and 10.
data e1_leads_said: NonEmptyStr = "pin 7 is 0v, pin 8 is ~1.8v"

data e1_leads_photo: EvidenceRef = e1_photo(taken_on: "2026-10-19", locator: "bench-session upload 64ce6dce, U1_P5 upright and straight down, no wire, leads 1 to 14 of the left-hand row (not on Drive)")

data e1_pin7_return_said: NonEmptyStr = "ok so basically, when black is on p7 ,and red is on J20ground, I see ~535, and reverse its >2k"

fn e1_lead_volts(pin: NonEmptyStr, millivolts: Nat) -> NodeVoltageObservation {
  NodeVoltageObservation {
    asset: p4261_e1_b, at: e1_terminal(c: e1_u1_p5, name: pin), reference: e1_ground_ref,
    record: second_point_inferred(basis: "the sheet's setup: the meter's black probe on J20's black lead, which joins J20's latch-side row; position 1 stands for the row"),
    conditions: e1_live_bench, source: volt(count: 48), value: ReadAbout { value: millivolt(count: millivolts) }, certainty: StatedPlainly,
    order: AfterIncidents { keys: [e1_bridge_incident.key] },
    evidence: [OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: e1_leads_said }],
  }
}

fn e1_pin7_to_return(polarity: ProbePolarity, range: MeterRange, display: ResistanceDisplay, said: NonEmptyStr) -> ResistanceObservation {
  ResistanceObservation {
    asset: p4261_e1_b, first: e1_terminal(c: e1_u1_p5, name: "pin 7"), second: e1_ground_ref,
    record: second_point_inferred(basis: "'J20ground': J20's black lead, which joins J20's latch-side row; position 1 stands for the row"),
    conditions: e1_bench, polarity: polarity, range: range, display: display, stability: StabilityUnrecorded, certainty: StatedPlainly,
    order: AfterIncidents { keys: [e1_bridge_incident.key] },
    evidence: [OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: said }, e1_leads_photo],
  }
}

data e1_pin7_lead_resistances: List<ResistanceObservation> = [
  e1_pin7_to_return(polarity: RedOnSecond, range: RangeFullScale { ohms: 200 }, display: DisplayOverRange, said: "G1 - large"),
  e1_pin7_to_return(polarity: RedOnFirst, range: RangeFullScale { ohms: 200 }, display: DisplayOverRange, said: "G2 - large"),
  e1_pin7_to_return(polarity: RedOnSecond, range: RangeUnrecorded, display: DisplayValue { ohms: 535, approximate: true }, said: e1_pin7_return_said),
  e1_pin7_to_return(polarity: RedOnFirst, range: RangeFullScale { ohms: 2000 }, display: DisplayOverRange, said: e1_pin7_return_said),
  e1_pin7_to_return(polarity: RedOnFirst, range: RangeFullScale { ohms: 20000 }, display: DisplayValue { ohms: 11000, approximate: true }, said: "G2 - yes, it was ~11k"),
]

// THE THIRD WIRE AND THE BACK-SIDE PADS. A third wire, W4, taped at the left-hand row with an alligator
// clip on its far end, read about 11 kohm to ground -- pin 7's own signature with the red probe on it --
// and 16 kohm to pin 8's back-side pad, so it is not on pin 8. Its join to pin 7's lead could not be
// read: the tape covers the leads. Flipped, three bare pads behind U1_P5 read 0 ohm from it (P5, P6, P7
// of a labelled photograph of the cluster beside Q5_P5 and D5_P5); flipped back, it read about 12 kohm to
// ground, so it stayed put. So P5 to P7 are pin 7's by the wire's signature, not by a baseline join to
// the lead. The cluster's pads carry no parts, and the same cluster is bare on the K1 (photograph): its
// empty places are the design's, not a part missing from the E1.
data e1_w4: ComponentInstanceIdentity = e1_component(local: "W4: wire taped at U1_P5's left-hand row, far end in an alligator clip")

data e1_w4_end: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_w4, name: "(far end)")

data e1_w4_said: NonEmptyStr = "ok i got a wire on pin 7 - it reads 11k to ground right now - i have an alligator clip on it, so i won't have to disturb that probe too much"

data e1_back_cluster: ComponentInstanceIdentity = e1_component(local: "bare pad cluster on the back beside Q5_P5 and D5_P5, behind U1_P5 (pads P1 to P10 as labelled)")

data e1_back_cluster_photo: EvidenceRef = e1_photo(taken_on: "2026-10-19", locator: "bench-session upload 75c33d9a, the back behind U1_P5 with P5 to P7 circled; labelled crop e1_back_pads_labeled (not on Drive)")

data e1_back_pads_said: NonEmptyStr = "I got a reading of 0 ohms to these three pads , everything else is consistent - to the known pin 8 pad is 16k, ground is still 12k"

// The operator's ruling: P6, which W4 read 0 ohm to, is pin 7's node. It settles W4's attachment in
// the record; no reading joins W4 or P6 to pin 7's lead, and with no baseline recorded the 0 ohm does
// not join W4 to P6 either.
data e1_p6_ruling_said: NonEmptyStr = "yes i am hyper confident that p6 == pin 7, please record this so we don't relitigate it again"

data e1_w4_attachment: ProbeAttachment = ProbeAttachment {
  point: e1_w4_end,
  intended: e1_terminal(c: e1_u1_p5, name: "pin 7"),
  statement: OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: e1_w4_said },
  disputes: [],
  ruling: [OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: e1_p6_ruling_said }],
}

fn e1_w4_read(to: ElectricalTerminalRef, polarity: ProbePolarity, range: MeterRange, display: ResistanceDisplay, said: NonEmptyStr, photo: List<EvidenceRef>) -> ResistanceObservation {
  ResistanceObservation {
    asset: p4261_e1_b, first: e1_w4_end, second: to,
    record: second_point_inferred(basis: "the point the sheet named, the operator's words naming the result"),
    conditions: e1_bench, polarity: polarity, range: range, display: display, stability: StabilityUnrecorded, certainty: StatedPlainly,
    order: AfterIncidents { keys: [e1_bridge_incident.key] },
    evidence: concat([OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: said }], photo),
  }
}

data e1_w4_resistances: List<ResistanceObservation> = [
  e1_w4_read(to: e1_ground_ref, polarity: PolarityUnrecorded, range: RangeUnrecorded, display: DisplayValue { ohms: 11000, approximate: true }, said: e1_w4_said, photo: []),
  e1_w4_read(to: e1_terminal(c: e1_ovlo_pad, name: "pad"), polarity: RedOnFirst, range: RangeUnrecorded, display: DisplayValue { ohms: 16000, approximate: false }, said: e1_back_pads_said, photo: []),
  e1_w4_read(to: e1_terminal(c: e1_back_cluster, name: "P5"), polarity: RedOnFirst, range: RangeUnrecorded, display: DisplayZeroWithoutBaseline { reported: "0 ohms" }, said: e1_back_pads_said, photo: [e1_back_cluster_photo]),
  e1_w4_read(to: e1_terminal(c: e1_back_cluster, name: "P6"), polarity: RedOnFirst, range: RangeUnrecorded, display: DisplayZeroWithoutBaseline { reported: "0 ohms" }, said: e1_back_pads_said, photo: [e1_back_cluster_photo]),
  e1_w4_read(to: e1_terminal(c: e1_back_cluster, name: "P7"), polarity: RedOnFirst, range: RangeUnrecorded, display: DisplayZeroWithoutBaseline { reported: "0 ohms" }, said: e1_back_pads_said, photo: [e1_back_cluster_photo]),
  e1_w4_read(to: e1_ground_ref, polarity: RedOnFirst, range: RangeUnrecorded, display: DisplayValue { ohms: 12000, approximate: true }, said: e1_back_pads_said, photo: []),
]

// THE CLUSTER'S OTHER PADS. Unpowered, each bare pad other than P5 to P7 read to J20's black lead
// (ground), to J20's red lead (the input side) and to the top end of pin 21's beige part (VDD's point):
// P10 is reported as ground ("p10 is ground", no baseline recorded); P1 to P4, P8 and P9 read above the baseline to all three, as
// P10 does to the red lead. So no pad of the cluster joins pin 7's pads to the return, to the input or
// to VDD directly; P9, beside the grounded P10, reads to none of them.
data e1_cluster_said: NonEmptyStr = "Basically what I'm seeing is p10 is ground, the rest are far"

data e1_cluster_vdd_said: NonEmptyStr = "i tried that top part to all the pads on the bottom but didn't see any thing close"

data e1_cluster_rows_basis: NonEmptyStr = "the sheet's X1 / X2: J20's black lead (latch-side row) or J20's red lead (fused row); position 1 stands for each row"

data e1_cluster_vdd_basis: NonEmptyStr = "'that top part': the sheet's X3, the top end of the beige part across from pin 21, marked on the operator's photograph"

fn e1_cluster_read(pad: NonEmptyStr, to: ElectricalTerminalRef, display: ResistanceDisplay, basis: NonEmptyStr, said: NonEmptyStr) -> ResistanceObservation {
  ResistanceObservation {
    asset: p4261_e1_b, first: e1_terminal(c: e1_back_cluster, name: pad), second: to,
    record: second_point_inferred(basis: basis),
    conditions: e1_bench, polarity: PolarityUnrecorded, range: RangeUnrecorded, display: display, stability: StabilityUnrecorded, certainty: StatedPlainly,
    order: AfterIncidents { keys: [e1_bridge_incident.key] },
    evidence: [OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: said }, e1_back_cluster_photo],
  }
}

data e1_cluster_resistances: List<ResistanceObservation> = concat(
  flat_map(["P1", "P2", "P3", "P4", "P8", "P9"], p => [
    e1_cluster_read(pad: p, to: e1_ground_ref, display: DisplayAboveBaseline, basis: e1_cluster_rows_basis, said: e1_cluster_said),
    e1_cluster_read(pad: p, to: e1_rail_ref, display: DisplayAboveBaseline, basis: e1_cluster_rows_basis, said: e1_cluster_said),
    e1_cluster_read(pad: p, to: e1_beige_top, display: DisplayAboveBaseline, basis: e1_cluster_vdd_basis, said: e1_cluster_vdd_said),
  ]),
  [
    e1_cluster_read(pad: "P10", to: e1_ground_ref, display: DisplayZeroWithoutBaseline { reported: "ground" }, basis: e1_cluster_rows_basis, said: e1_cluster_said),
    e1_cluster_read(pad: "P10", to: e1_rail_ref, display: DisplayAboveBaseline, basis: e1_cluster_rows_basis, said: e1_cluster_said),
  ],
)

// Q301 AND Q300. Unpowered, the lone lead of Q301's three-lead package on the back reads 0.00 ohm
// to P6 -- pin 7's by the third wire's signature and the operator's ruling, not by a reading. Q301's
// lead a reads 0 ohm and Q300's lead a 0.00 ohm to J20's return, and Q301's lead b 0.00 ohm to Q300's
// lone lead (leads named by place on the labelled photograph). No baseline or range was recorded, so
// each is a reported zero and the netlist keeps its points apart. Both parts carry 'K38', a candidate
// for Diodes Incorporated's BSS138 (e1_k38_candidate), so which terminal each lead is stays a lead.
data e1_q301: ComponentInstanceIdentity = e1_component(local: "Q301")

data e1_q301_lone_lead: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_q301, name: "lone lead of its three-lead package")

data e1_q301_lead_a: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_q301, name: "lead a: two-lead side, away from the silkscreen triangle")

data e1_q301_lead_b: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_q301, name: "lead b: two-lead side, beside the silkscreen triangle")

data e1_q300: ComponentInstanceIdentity = e1_component(local: "Q300")

data e1_q300_lone_lead: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_q300, name: "lone lead of its three-lead package")

data e1_q300_lead_a: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_q300, name: "lead a: two-lead side, away from the silkscreen triangle")

data e1_k38_photo: EvidenceRef = e1_photo(taken_on: "2026-10-19", locator: "bench-session upload 42ffb97b, Q300 and Q301 both marked K38, and the resistor beside Q301 with its marking, first read as 180 (not on Drive)")

// Q300 and Q301 carry 'K38', Diodes Incorporated's BSS138 product marking code (DS30144). Another maker
// may use the same code, and the photograph shows no date-code line, so the identification is a
// candidate. Under that row's pinout and the silkscreen triangle on pin 1, lead b would be the gate,
// lead a the source and the lone lead the drain -- which the readings fit, and which they do not prove.
data e1_k38_candidate: ComponentIdentification = MarkingCandidate {
  row: bss138,
  marking: MarkingReading { text: "K38", evidence: e1_k38_photo },
  discriminator: "the maker's date-code line, or another maker's marking table, read against Diodes Incorporated's BSS138 table",
}

data e1_q300_q301_photo: EvidenceRef = e1_photo(taken_on: "2026-10-19", locator: "bench-session upload 9d88e42f, Q300 and Q301 on the back; leads labelled in the crop q300_q301_labeled (not on Drive)")

data e1_q300_q301_said: NonEmptyStr = "Q301-a J20black: 0ohm, Q301-b to Q300 lone: 0.00ohm, Q300-a to J20 black: 0.00ohm"

// THE RESISTOR ON Q301'S LEAD B, AND ITS FAR END. Unpowered, the end of the resistor beside Q301 (R on
// the labelled photograph; its marking, first read as '180', reads '18D' enlarged) nearer Q301 is
// reported equal to Q301's lead b ('==', no display or baseline recorded). The operator followed its far end's trace by eye to the front: along the board edge under Q21_P5 and
// Q22_P5 toward D5's tab, past a pair of large bare pads, and up the left edge past the bare U2_P5 and
// U3_P5 footprints toward U1_TSE beside J1 (two annotated photographs). From the far end they read 0 ohm
// along that route as far as about U2_P5 and about 2 kohm beyond it toward J1, the points named only by
// place. They read the layout as two input sides, J1's backplane and J20 -- their reading, not a
// measurement.
data e1_q301_resistor: ComponentInstanceIdentity = e1_component(local: "resistor beside Q301 (R on the labelled photograph)")

data e1_q301_resistor_near: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_q301_resistor, name: "end nearer Q301")

data e1_q301_resistor_far: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_q301_resistor, name: "far end")

data e1_route_near_u2: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_component(local: "front trace of the Q301 resistor's far end, as the operator traced it"), name: "point near U2_P5")

data e1_route_toward_j1: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_component(local: "front trace of the Q301 resistor's far end, as the operator traced it"), name: "point beyond U2_P5 toward J1")

data e1_route_said: NonEmptyStr = "Z2: the R other end traces back to this thing on the front - it also traces back towards J1 (2k ohms - 0 ohms until ~U2_P5) - I think there are two sides, one is the normal backplane -> j1, and one is towards j20"

data e1_route_photos: List<EvidenceRef> = [
  e1_photo(taken_on: "2026-10-19", locator: "bench-session upload a965dc18, the front under Q21_P5 / Q22_P5 with the far end's route drawn toward D5 (not on Drive)"),
  e1_photo(taken_on: "2026-10-19", locator: "bench-session upload 1cad7388, the front's left edge with the far end's route drawn past U2_P5 toward U1_TSE and J1 (not on Drive)"),
]

fn e1_route_read(to: ElectricalTerminalRef, display: ResistanceDisplay, certainty: StatementCertainty) -> ResistanceObservation {
  ResistanceObservation {
    asset: p4261_e1_b, first: e1_q301_resistor_far, second: to,
    record: second_point_inferred(basis: "a point on the route the operator drew, named by place only"),
    conditions: e1_bench, polarity: PolarityUnrecorded, range: RangeUnrecorded, display: display, stability: StabilityUnrecorded, certainty: certainty,
    order: AfterIncidents { keys: [e1_bridge_incident.key] },
    evidence: concat([OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: e1_route_said }], e1_route_photos),
  }
}

// THE VIA ON Q301'S LEAD B, ENERGIZED. The via between Q301's lead b and Q300's lone lead ('via' on the
// labelled photograph, on that node by the visible trace, not by a reading) read about 3.8 V with the
// source at 38 V and about 4.9 V at 54 V, against J20's black lead: it rises with the input, not in
// proportion to it. Under the common SOT-23 pinout lead b is a gate or base, where a few volts would
// switch a small transistor on; the K38 parts are unidentified, so that stays a lead.
data e1_q301_b_via: ElectricalTerminalRef = e1_terminal(c: e1_component(local: "via between Q301's lead b and Q300's lone lead ('via' on the labelled photograph)"), name: "via pad")

data e1_q301_b_via_said: NonEmptyStr = "The v1: that via node changes depending on the input voltage - input 38v: ~3.8v on via pad, input 54v:4.9v / V1: is the ID from your earlier message - that was the via pad i probed for that"

fn e1_via_volts(source_volts: Nat, millivolts: Nat, certainty: StatementCertainty) -> NodeVoltageObservation {
  NodeVoltageObservation {
    asset: p4261_e1_b, at: e1_q301_b_via, reference: e1_ground_ref,
    record: second_point_inferred(basis: "the sheet's V1: the meter's black probe on J20's black lead, which joins J20's latch-side row; position 1 stands for the row"),
    conditions: e1_live_bench, source: volt(count: source_volts), value: ReadAbout { value: millivolt(count: millivolts) }, certainty: certainty,
    order: AfterIncidents { keys: [e1_bridge_incident.key] },
    evidence: [OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: e1_q301_b_via_said }, e1_q300_q301_photo],
  }
}

fn e1_q_read(a: ElectricalTerminalRef, b: ElectricalTerminalRef, reported: NonEmptyStr) -> ResistanceObservation {
  ResistanceObservation {
    asset: p4261_e1_b, first: a, second: b,
    record: both_points_recorded,
    conditions: e1_bench, polarity: PolarityUnrecorded, range: RangeUnrecorded, display: DisplayZeroWithoutBaseline { reported: reported }, stability: StabilityUnrecorded, certainty: StatedPlainly,
    order: AfterIncidents { keys: [e1_bridge_incident.key] },
    evidence: [OperatorStatement { stated_on: "2026-10-19", verbatim: e1_q300_q301_said }, e1_q300_q301_photo],
  }
}

data e1_q301_resistances: List<ResistanceObservation> = [
  ResistanceObservation {
    asset: p4261_e1_b, first: e1_q301_lone_lead, second: e1_terminal(c: e1_back_cluster, name: "P6"),
    record: both_points_recorded,
